    "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a BioSemi ActiveTwo system (72 channels, 2048 Hz; CMS at Cz, DRL at Fz) during a visual roving oddball task using face stimuli from the FACES database, processed with webmorphR and SHINE. Fixation cross colour signalled whether a response was required on catch trials. After the EEG session, participants rated each face on Self-Assessment Manikin valence, arousal and dominance scales (1-5). Derivatives were produced with MNE-Python (filtering, ICA correction, epoching).",
